1. every expression's value is echoed, one per line:
   in:  1 + 1
   in:  x = 2
   in:  x * 3
   in:  _
   in:  [1, 2].map { it * 2 }
   in:  puts "side effect"
   in:  nil
   in:  def f(x) = x * 2
   in:  f(21)
   out: 2
   out: 2
   out: 6
   out: 6
   out: [2, 4]
   out: side effect
   out: nil
   out: nil
   out: :f
   out: 42
   stderr empty: true   exit: 0
2. an error is printed and the session goes on:
   in:  1 / 0
   in:  "after"
   out: (irb):1:in 'Integer#/': divided by 0 (ZeroDivisionError)
   out: 	from (irb):1:in '<main>'
   out: 	from -e:1:in '<main>'
   out: "after"
   stderr empty: true   exit: 0
3. --noecho keeps only what the code prints itself:
   in:  1 + 1
   in:  puts "side effect"
   out: side effect
   stderr empty: true   exit: 0
4. exit ends the session; later lines are never read:
   in:  puts "before"
   in:  exit
   in:  puts "never"
   out: before
   out: nil
   stderr empty: true   exit: 0
